          "path": "_m/g/c/e/y/belfast-castle-wp/pen-ink-sketch-belfast.png",
          "filename": "Ground Plan of Belfast (1685).png",
          "caption": "A pen and ink sketch of Belfast, prepared as part of Thomas Phillips' survey of Irish towns and fortifications. The town's existing ramparts are overlaid by a much grander scheme of Phillips' own devisal, with a plan for a citadel to the north. Landmarks include Belfast Castle and the Corporation Church, and the unfinished Long Bridge. The River Farset runs through the High Street and the Blackstaff flows over the slobland to the south, meeting the Lagan via the \"new cutt\".",
          "alt": "A pen and ink sketch of Belfast, prepared as part of Thomas Phillips' survey of Irish towns and fortifications. The town's existing ramparts are overlaid by a much grander scheme of Phillips' own devisal, with a plan for a citadel to the north. Landmarks include Belfast Castle and the Corporation Church, and the unfinished Long Bridge. The River Farset runs through the High Street and the Blackstaff flows over the slobland to the south, meeting the Lagan via the \"new cutt\".",
