        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/e/y/belfast-castle-wp/belfast-castle-belfast-co-antr.jpg",
          "filename": "Belfast Castle, Belfast, Co. Antrim (21183016023).jpg",
          "caption": "From one great rock (that caught the Dunbrody) to another which anchors Belfast Castle.\nWith thanks to all our contributors below, we've learned a little more about the 19th century design and construction of Belfast Castle - and had our interest piqued by the left-field reference which Sharon notes in the Dictionary of Irish Architects:\n\n Name [architect]: LANYON, LYNN &amp; LANYON\n Building: CO. ANTRIM, BELFAST, BELFAST CASTLE\n Date: 1868-70\n Nature: New Scottish Baronial house on slope of Cave Hill by John Lanyon, for Marquess of Donegall. Faced with Cookstown stone with white Scottish stone dressings. \n Name [architect]: SEAVER, HENRY\n Building: CO. ANTRIM, BELFAST, BELFAST CASTLE\n Date: 1922a\n Nature: HS [Henry Seaver] said to have 'waved his Prospero's wand' over Belfast Castle.\n\nPhotographer: Unknown\nCollection:  Eason Photographic Collection\nDate: between ca. 1900-1939\nNLI Ref:  EAS_0524\n\nYou can also view this image, and many thousands of others, on the NLI’s catalogue at catalogue.nli.ie",
          "alt": "From one great rock (that caught the Dunbrody) to another which anchors Belfast Castle.\nWith thanks to all our contributors below, we've learned a little more about the 19th century design and construction of Belfast Castle - and had our interest piqued by the left-field reference which Sharon notes in the Dictionary of Irish Architects:\n\n Name [architect]: LANYON, LYNN &amp; LANYON\n Building: CO. ANTRIM, BELFAST, BELFAST CASTLE\n Date: 1868-70\n Nature: New Scottish Baronial house on slope of Cave Hill by John Lanyon, for Marquess of Donegall. Faced with Cookstown stone with white Scottish stone dressings. \n Name [architect]: SEAVER, HENRY\n Building: CO. ANTRIM, BELFAST, BELFAST CASTLE\n Date: 1922a\n Nature: HS [Henry Seaver] said to have 'waved his Prospero's wand' over Belfast Castle.\n\nPhotographer: Unknown\nCollection:  Eason Photographic Collection\nDate: between ca. 1900-1939\nNLI Ref:  EAS_0524\n\nYou can also view this image, and many thousands of others, on the NLI’s catalogue at catalogue.nli.ie",
          "width": 2000,
          "height": 1438,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "Public domain",
          "artist": "National Library of Ireland on The Commons",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belfast_Castle,_Belfast,_Co._Antrim_(21183016023).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "belfast-castle-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "gcey",
